On Wed, Jan 2, 2013 at 11:36 PM, Jonathan Jones <eyeonus@gmail.com> wrote:

> On Wed, Jan 2, 2013 at 3:13 PM, Remo Dentato <rdentato@gmail.com> wrote:
>
>> You failed to notice that they are not regular at all as three glosses
>> you wrote are all different.
>>
>
> No I didn't. They are "different" because the -bo'e of each have different
> amount of sumti places: gasnu has 2, mutce 3, and traji 4.
>
Yes, that's what makes them different and what makes them non regular.

First of all, it's not my rule, and second of all, it's not a "so-called"
> rule, it's an actual rule. It's part of the CLL, in Chapter 12, although
> I'm not going to bother trying to find the exact section.
>

I've Chapter 12 in front of me and I cant find it. Instead in section 12.1
(I bothered looking for it) you can read:

"There are no absolute laws fixing the place structure of a newly created
lujvo. The
maker must consider the place structures of all the components of the tanru
and
then decide which are still relevant and which can be removed. What is said
in this
chapter represents guidelines, presented as one possible standard, not
necessarily
complete, and not the only possible standard."

So if we want to make a rule for jvajvo we should at least try to make it
clear to everyone.

